invariant: INV-16
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: table_select writes each mask through its volatile pointer and
  then uses the value it computed and not the one it would read back, so
  the compiler still knows which entry the mask keeps. The pinned clang
  happens to emit no branch for this form on either 64-bit spec, so the
  branch count passes, and another compiler or another release is free
  to test the two positions as clang did for the form with no pointer.
  inv-16-rsa-table-read refuses a mask in table_select that is taken
  straight from mask_of_bit.

--- old
        *hidden = mask_of_bit(differ ^ 1);
        uint64_t mask = *hidden;
--- new
        uint64_t mask = mask_of_bit(differ ^ 1);
        *hidden = mask;
